# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Experiments ran on an NVIDIA GeForce RTX A4000 (16 GB). Training time,
# inference time, parameter counts and FLOPs are compared in Figure 4
# (LEIGNN about ten times faster than GemNet-dT and MACE); no number is
# printed.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Hyperparameters of all eight models are in the Supplementary Material (Section 3) and are not encoded, nor are the loss weights alpha and beta.
# - 'PaiNN Direct' is PaiNN with direct force prediction and is encoded under entity:PaiNN with a 'force-mode' setting; GemNet-dT under entity:GemNet with its variant setting; DimeNet++ under entity:DimeNet.
# - The ablation study (Table 2, OC20-50K and OC20-200K), the MD17 and ISO17 comparisons of the supplement, and the MD simulation benchmark of Table 3 are not encoded.
# - Energy MAEs are in meV per structure (adsorption energies). The four validation sets are modelled as material systems so that errors group by split, as in chanussot2021 (whose nodes are not reused; they are paper-local).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

